        <item>
            <title>0.2</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 08 Aug 2026 09:43:09 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>501</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.2</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
p { margin: 4px 0 10px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.2 (build 501)</h2>
<p><b>Color follows the grader — on every seat, including the web.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>Grades follow live in hosted sessions.</b> Adjust exposure, CDL or looks and every connected Asobi — internal or Review — re-applies the same grade in its own color pipeline, so an EXR seat and an optimized-media seat land on the same picture. Late joiners receive the room's grade on arrival. Look files travel with the grade; a look a seat can't be given is dropped there, never guessed at.</li>
<li><b>Web pages follow as a live trim</b> — a small display-referred correction applied over their streamed video in WebGL, the way a DIT trims through a monitor path. Immediate and faithful in the mids; blind to highlights their proxy already clipped.</li>
<li><b>New: File ▸ Update Web Share with Current Grades</b> re-renders shared clips with grades baked in — exact web pixels, minutes not milliseconds, and the page retires its live trim for those clips automatically so nothing applies twice.</li>
<li><b>The grade tools tell you about web viewers.</b> Review Grade and Film Lab show a banner whenever web seats are connected: following approximately, not following (toggle off), or unable to follow — each with the remedy named.</li>
<li><b>All of it is switchable</b> in Settings ▸ Color ▸ Color to Other Seats, and Settings itself has been redesigned — tinted section icons, clearer grouping, and footers that explain what each control actually does.</li>
<li><b>Fixed: exposure meant different things on different media.</b> +1 EV on an optimized stand-in rendered 80/255 brighter than the same EV on the EXR. Exposure now applies in scene-linear whatever the media, which grade-follow made mandatory: a grade must be one picture on every seat.</li>
<li>The manual covers all of the above (expert chapters 5 and 10, client chapter 3).</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
